---
description: Always use uv for Python, never venv or pip
alwaysApply: true
---

# Python: uv only

- Use `uv` for all Python work: `uv init`, `uv add`, `uv run`, `uv sync`.
- Never create a `.venv` with `python -m venv` or `virtualenv`.
- Never install with `pip` / `pip3` (no `--break-system-packages` either).
- Run scripts with `uv run python ...` so dependencies come from the project env uv manages.
